.TH MX-DATETIME 1 "2026-07-20" "MX Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mx-datetime \- manage system and hardware clock settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mx-datetime
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mx-datetime
provides a graphical interface for managing the system date, time, time zone, and hardware clock. Changes to the system or hardware clock are applied only when the corresponding action is confirmed.
.PP
The hardware-clock controls can transfer the system time to the hardware clock or transfer the hardware-clock time to the system clock. The application can read the hardware clock and apply drift corrections when a drift factor is known. The hardware clock can be configured to use UTC or local time; UTC is recommended when the machine is not shared with an operating system that requires local hardware-clock time.
.PP
When run without root privileges, the application uses Slender Mode. This mode provides a calendar and clock for comparing time zones without allowing changes to the system or hardware clock.
.SH OPTIONS
This application has no documented command-line options. The graphical interface provides all operations.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/mx-datetime
Installed HTML help, images, license, and changelog documentation.
.SH AUTHOR
MX Linux contributors.
